pi-coding-agent for Debian
=========================

Source format: 3.0 (native).

Network requirement
--------------------
The build needs network access to the npm registry. Two `npm install` calls
fetch packages:

  * override_dh_auto_configure: `npm install --ignore-scripts` hydrates the
    workspace dev toolchain (tsgo, shx, vitest, ...).
  * debian/stage: `npm install --omit=dev --ignore-scripts` installs the
    third-party runtime deps of @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent into the
    staging tree.

`node_modules/` and the compiled `packages/*/dist` trees are therefore not
part of the source package (excluded via debian/source/options); they are
regenerated during the build.

Near-offline builds
-------------------
To build without live network access, pre-populate the npm cache first from a
networked machine, then point the build at it:

    npm install --ignore-scripts          # warm ~/.npm/_cacache
    # copy ~/.npm/_cacache onto the build host, then:
    HOME=<home-with-cache> dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Both `npm install` invocations resolve from the cache when the registry is
unreachable.

Generated model data
---------------------
packages/ai imports per-provider model values from
packages/ai/src/providers/data/*.json. These are generated (gitignored) by
`npm --prefix packages/ai run generate-models`, which also fetches live model
lists from non-npm endpoints (openrouter.ai, models.dev, ...). They are not
part of the git tree and are not excluded by debian/source/options, so they
ship in the native source tarball only if present on disk at `dpkg-source -b`
time.

override_dh_auto_build regenerates data/ on demand *only when absent*, using
the generator's --json-only mode (writes the JSON values without rewriting
the committed *.models.ts / models.generated.ts catalogs, so the tree is not
churned). A binary build from a bare checkout therefore needs network access
to those model-list endpoints.

Official buildds have no such network. Pre-generate the data on a networked
machine so it is baked into the source tarball, where the binary build finds
it already present and skips regeneration entirely:

    npm --prefix packages/ai run generate-models   # refreshes committed catalogs; commit any drift
    dpkg-source -b .

Tests
-----
override_dh_auto_test does not run the upstream suite. The suite needs Node's
TypeScript stripper (tui: `node --test *.ts`; ai: a `node --eval` probe over
.ts sources), which Debian's nodejs is built without (ERR_NO_TYPESCRIPT). A
`pi --version` smoke test runs instead; the full suite runs in upstream CI.
